TITLE:: InsightSpectrum
summary:: one FFT frame folded into log spaced bands, with falling traces
categories:: Libraries>Insight
related:: Classes/Insight, Classes/InsightLoudness, Classes/FFT

DESCRIPTION::
The spectrum half of link::Classes/Insight::, on its own. A synth does one link::Classes/FFT:: and nothing else - it fills a buffer and never reads it back - and the language fetches that buffer a frame at a time and hands it here. This takes the loudest bin in each of its log spaced bands, which is the point of reducing it in the language rather than on the server: a band near the top of the range covers a hundred bins, and a tone in it is in one of them.

code::
sp = InsightSpectrum(4096, 48000);
sp.take(frame, 0.066);         // a frame from b_getn, and the seconds since the last
sp.levels;                     // dB per band, falling at fallDb a second
sp.peaks;                      // the same, falling slower
sp.maxima;                     // the loudest in each band since resetMaxima
sp.freqs;                      // the frequency each band sits at
::

Three traces, so the picture says three things at once: what is there now, what was there a moment ago, and the loudest there has been since the last reset. code::smoothing:: averages the power first, for a display that moves like a slow analyser. A full scale sine through the Hann window peaks at N/4 in its bin, so that is where 0 dB is.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: fftSize
the FFT size the frames come from.
ARGUMENT:: sampleRate
the rate the server is running at, which sets where each bin sits.
RETURNS:: an InsightSpectrum.

METHOD:: numBands
How many bands are kept, log spaced. 128 by default.

METHOD:: minFreq
METHOD:: maxFreq
The ends of the range, 20 Hz to 20 kHz.

METHOD:: fallDb
METHOD:: peakFallDb
How fast the two falling traces fall, in dB a second.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

private:: prBandBins

METHOD:: take
Fold one frame into the bands and let the traces fall.
ARGUMENT:: frame
the buffer contents: DC at 0, nyquist at 1, then bin k as the pair at 2k and 2k+1.
ARGUMENT:: dt
seconds since the last frame, so the falls are per second however fast frames arrive.
RETURNS:: this.

METHOD:: levels
METHOD:: peaks
METHOD:: maxima
dB per band: the current trace, the slower one, and the held maximum.

METHOD:: freqs
The centre frequency of each band.

METHOD:: fetchCount
How many values of a frame are worth reading: up to the top of the drawn range.

METHOD:: levelAt
METHOD:: maximumAt
The trace, or the held maximum, at a frequency - the band it falls in.
ARGUMENT:: freq
a frequency in Hz.

METHOD:: posOf
METHOD:: freqAt
Between 0 and 1 across the range, and back: what a grid line and a hover readout want.

METHOD:: smoothing
The display average, 0 to 0.95.

METHOD:: floorDb
METHOD:: topDb
The ends of the dB scale.

METHOD:: hold
Whether to keep the per-band maxima.

METHOD:: reset
Clear the traces and the maxima.

METHOD:: resetMaxima
Clear just the held maxima.

METHOD:: clear
Clear the moving traces, keeping the maxima - what a stop shows.
